olling or a surge of outside spending against Ryan could narrow the margin if the residency attacks gain traction.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Pat Ryan (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Pat Ryan, the Democratic incumbent in a Hudson Valley district that leans about two points Democratic, is seeking reelection against Republican Jacqueline Auringer. Ryan has raised more than $4.7 million and holds over $3.1 million on hand, while Auringer has raised under $90,000 with no reported outside support. Recent polls, all sponsored by Democratic-leaning firms, show Ryan ahead by 9 to 17 points among likely voters.\n\nPrediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket both price Ryan's win probability at roughly 95-96%. The campaign has featured attacks over Ryan's residency and sharp exchanges both candidates called beyond the pale, but no evidence suggests those are moving the race materially. Ryan's incumbency, financial dominance, and the favorable polling point to a comfortable expected margin of about 15 points, with residual uncertainty from the partisan sponsorship of available polls.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 17.1}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.971, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9767, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9844, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9723, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.971, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.978, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9814, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9828, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9869, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9867, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9709, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.972, "margin": 15.0}